{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nepotistic-sensitive-arcticwolf","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\n\nA full `make verify` on macOS arm64 (2026-10-27, `PYTEST_WORKERS=4`, worktree branched from `ee5253abfd4`) ended:\n\n```\n22 failed, 19835 passed, 88 skipped, 48 warnings, 1 error in 5467.30s (1:31:07)\n```\n\nAll 22 failures, and the 1 error, are in four files that drive `infra/scripts/observability.sh`:\n\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_health_9ea3.py` (9 failures + the error)\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py` (2)\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py` (1)\n- `tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_markers.py` (1)\n\nplus the parameterised cases of `test_an_unhealthy_serving_path_publishes_zero_not_nothing`.\n\nThe captured stderr names the cause directly:\n\n```\ninfra/scripts/observability.sh: line 160: /var/lib/rebar/probe-region: No such file or directory\ninfra/scripts/observability.sh: line 230: /var/lib/rebar/reviewbot-webhook-auth-offset: No such file or directory\nsubprocess.TimeoutExpired: Command '['bash', '.../infra/scripts/observability.sh']'\n  timed out after 59.99996245803777 seconds\n```\n\n`/var/lib/rebar/` does not exist on macOS and is not creatable by an unprivileged user. The script's writes fail, and the run then exceeds the tests' own 60 s `subprocess.run(..., timeout=60)` bound, so the failure surfaces as a timeout rather than as the missing-path error that actually caused it.\n\n## Why these defaults are reached at all\n\n`infra/scripts/observability.sh` defaults several state-file paths under `/var/lib/rebar`:\n\n```\nREGION_CACHE=\"${REGION_CACHE:-/var/lib/rebar/probe-region}\"\nREVIEWBOT_WEBHOOK_AUTH_OFFSET_FILE=\"${REVIEWBOT_WEBHOOK_AUTH_OFFSET_FILE:-/var/lib/rebar/reviewbot-webhook-auth-offset}\"\nGATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT=\"${GATE_SCRATCH_MOUNT:-/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch}\"\nGATE_SCRATCH_VOLUME_ID_FILE=\"${GATE_SCRATCH_VOLUME_ID_FILE:-/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch-volume-id}\"\nREPL_OFFSET_FILE=\"${REPL_OFFSET_FILE:-/var/lib/rebar/repl-fail-offset}\"\n```\n\nEach is overridable by environment variable, and the tests build an environment with `_environment(tmp_path, ...)` — so the pattern for redirecting them into `tmp_path` already exists. **At least `REGION_CACHE` and `REVIEWBOT_WEBHOOK_AUTH_OFFSET_FILE` are not among the ones the tests override**, which is why the real host path is reached. Whether the remaining three are covered has not been checked.\n\n## Not established\n\n- Whether these tests pass on Linux CI because `/var/lib/rebar` exists there, or because the runner can create it. `main` is green on `ubuntu-latest`, so they pass there by some means; which means has not been measured.\n- Whether the 60 s test bound is also marginal on a loaded host independently of the missing directory — the timeout is a consequence of the failed writes here, but the two could compound.\n\n## Why this matters\n\n`make verify` is the stated pre-push contract and the locally checkable half of `Verified`. This is the **second independent reason** it cannot go green on an unmodified tree on arm64 macOS; the first is bug `degraded-chilly-galago` (`bb19-4776-46d2-4223`), the `pypandoc_binary` 1.17 arm64 wheel shipping an x86_64 pandoc. With the pandoc workaround applied, these 22 remain. An agent on this hardware therefore cannot satisfy the contract and learns to read a red `make verify` as normal, which is exactly the erosion the contract exists to prevent.\n\nIt also means bug `bb19`'s acceptance criterion \"`make verify` exits 0 on an unmodified tree on arm64 macOS\" is **not achievable by fixing pandoc alone**. That criterion needs this ticket closed too.\n\n## Approach\n\n1. Confirm the override gap by listing which of the five `/var/lib/rebar` defaults `_environment` sets and which it does not.\n2. Redirect every host-state path the script consults into `tmp_path` from the test environment, so no test writes outside its own fixture. This is a test-side fix: the production defaults are correct for the deployed Linux host and should not change.\n3. Re-check whether the 60 s subprocess bound is still adequate once the writes succeed; if the script legitimately needs longer on a loaded host, raise the bound rather than retry — a retry would mask the next regression.\n4. Do not mark these tests as Linux-only or skip them on macOS. A skip hides the portability gap instead of closing it, and the script's behaviour is the thing under test, not the host's directory layout.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every `/var/lib/rebar` default that `infra/scripts/observability.sh` reads is redirected into the test's `tmp_path`, verified by asserting that no file is created under `/var/lib/rebar` during the run.\n- [ ] `pytest tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_health_9ea3.py tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py tests/scripts/test_observability_marker_anchor_8c2f.py tests/scripts/test_observability_mcp_markers.py -q` passes on arm64 macOS with no manual host setup.\n- [ ] The production defaults in `infra/scripts/observability.sh` are unchanged, or any change to them is justified as a deployment improvement rather than a test accommodation.\n- [ ] No test is skipped or marked platform-specific to achieve the above.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on an unmodified tree on arm64 macOS, together with the fix for `bb19-4776-46d2-4223`.\n\nDiscovered 2026-10-27 during a `make verify` for bug `9cf1-3663-4de6-4844` (Gerrit change 3125), whose own diff touches neither `infra/` nor `tests/scripts/`.","id":"7f3d-ddc9-04d9-4861","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"make verify fails with 22 observability-script failures on arm64 macOS: tests reach /var/lib/rebar defaults"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793169300047227877,"uuid":"e6b81730-0dd0-4a05-b0f0-a33da3775ef3"}